  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 7 tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: 9 tests, 0 failed.\n\nHow it works:\n- **Diacritics:** `đ` and `Đ` are mapped to `d` first. The text is then split into base letters and combining marks (NFD) and the marks are removed.\n- **Case and separators:** the text is lowercased, and every run of characters outside `a-z` and `0-9` becomes a single hyphen.\n- **Hyphens and length:** leading and trailing hyphens are stripped, the result is cut to 50 characters, and any hyphen the cut leaves at the end is removed.\n\n`null` or `undefined` input returns an empty string.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- basic text and Vietnamese diacritics, including `đ`\n- other Latin diacritics\n- runs of separators and trimmed hyphens\n- empty and symbols-only input\n- the 50-character limit, including a cut that lands on a hyphen",
